 "changes": [
  "amount separators: a comma read as a full stop, or doubled, no longer breaks an amount; the thousands-group structure is still required",
  "second reading: a code or date that is not shaped like its field, or read below 70 confidence, is cropped, enlarged 3x and read again with a field-specific alphabet; accepted only when it is shaped like the field",
  "date unit marks: 년/월 read as a digit or letter are cut out only when exactly one cut gives a real calendar date",
  "leading code letter: '$' is repaired to S (only an S looks like it)"
